<article class="env-warning" id="00YP">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00YP">Warning <span data-tag="00YP">3.3.3.22</span>.</a> In the statement of Proposition <a data-tag="00YL" href="/tag/00YL">3.3.3.17</a>, the hypothesis that $X$ is braced cannot be omitted. For example, let $X$ be the simplicial set $\Delta ^{2} \coprod _{ \Delta ^{1} } \Delta ^0$ obtained from the standard $2$-simplex by collapsing a single edge, which we depict informally by the diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  &amp;  \bullet \ar [ddddrr] &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ \bullet \ar@ {=}[uuuurr] \ar [rrrr] &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \bullet .} \]
</div>
<p> Then the subdivision of $X$ is the $2$-dimensional simplicial set depicted in the diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  &amp;  \bullet \ar@ {=}[ddl] \ar [ddr] \ar [ddd] &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  &amp;  \\ &amp;  \bullet \ar [dr] &amp;  &amp;  \bullet \ar [dl] &amp;  \\ &amp;  &amp;  \bullet &amp;  &amp;  \\ \bullet \ar [urr] \ar [rr] \ar@ {=}[uur] &amp;  &amp;  \bullet \ar [u] &amp;  &amp;  \bullet . \ar [ll] \ar [ull] \ar [uul] } \]
</div>
<p> This simplicial set cannot arise as the nerve of a category, because it contains a nondegenerate $2$-simplex $\sigma $ for which $d^{2}_2(\sigma )$ is degenerate. </p>
</article>
